          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            By the
            %em Burnside category
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            one means either
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+correspondences"} category of correspondences
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
                (Prop.
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PermutativeCategoryOfFiniteGSets"}
                below)
            %li
              %p or an abelianization of that
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    either by
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion"} group completion
                    of its monoidal
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-groupoids"} hom-groupoids
                    to an
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-category"} 1-category
                    (Def.
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdditiveBurnsideCategory"}
                    below);
                %li
                  %p
                    or by forming the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+of+a+permutative+category"} K-theory of a permutative category
                    of the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-groupoids"} hom-groupoids
                    to a
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} spectra
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} enriched (∞,1)-category
                    (Def.
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpectralBurnsideCategory"}
                    below).
          %p
            The plain
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burnside+ring"} Burnside ring
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism+ring"} endomorphism ring
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-set"} G-set
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive
            version of the category (Example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#BurnsideRingIsEndomorphismRingInBurnsideCategory"}
            below).
          %p
            The
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+functors"} additive functors
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} enriched (∞,1)-functors
            from the Burnside category to, in particular, the
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+abelian+groups"} category of abelian groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+spectra"} (∞,1)-category of spectra
            are called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mackey+functors"} Mackey functors
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            out of the Burnside category is called a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mackey+functor"} Mackey functor
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
            out of the
            = succeed "-version" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectra"} spectra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
            out of the spectral Burnside category to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spectra"} Spectra
            is called a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+Mackey+functor"} spectral Mackey functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} equivalent
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genuine+G-spectra"} genuine G-spectra
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+stable+homotopy+theory"} equivariant stable homotopy theory
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            There are various incarnations of the Burnside category as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
            = succeed "\u201D." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmos"} cosmos
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure"} structure
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutative+categories"} permutative categories
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correspondences"} correspondences
            between two fixed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
            (made explicit as Prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PermutativeCategoryOfFiniteGSets"}
            below). This yields the Burnside category as
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a{:href => "#AsEnrichedInPermutativeCategories"} enriched in permutative categories
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a{:href => "#AsEnrichedInabelianGroups"} enriched in abelian groups
                ;
            %li
              %p
                %em>
                  %a{:href => "#EnrichedInSpectra"} enriched in spectra
                \.
          #PermutativeCategoryOfFiniteGSets.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutative+category"} permutative category
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+group"} finite group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mi sk
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G FinSet_{sk}
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleton"} skeleton
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
            %p
              Its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              may be identified with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,\rho)
              consisting of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite set
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{1,2, \cdots, n\}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group homomorphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho \;\colon\; G \longrightarrow S_n = Aut(\{1,2, \cdots, n\})
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+group"} symmetric group
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              elements, reflecting the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
              group of that finite set.
            %p
              Its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n_1,\rho_1) \overset{ f }{\longrightarrow} (n_2, \rho_2)
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi n
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \;\colon\; \{1, 2, \cdots, n_1\} \longrightarrow \{1,2, \cdots, n_2\}
              that intertwine
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_1
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ρ
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho_2
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproduct"} coproduct
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊔
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sqcup
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"}> disjoint union
              ) makes this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleton"} skeleton
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutative+category"} permutative category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %mi G
                      %msub
                        %mi FinSet
                        %mi sk
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \big( G FinSet_{sk}, \sqcup \big)
            %p
              In the same way its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+category"} slice category
              over any object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mi sk
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in G FinSet_{sk}
              becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutative+category"} permutative category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mi sk
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \big( G FinSet_{sk}/_{X}, \sqcup \big)
              under disjoint union of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domains"} domains
            %p
              Similarly, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              of finite
              = succeed "-sets" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleta"} skeleta
              to produce
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bipermutative+categories"} bipermutative categories
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %mi G
                      %msub
                        %mi FinSet
                        %mi sk
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \big( G FinSet_{sk}/_{X}, \sqcup, \times \big)
            %p
              Finally, restriction to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
              (passage to
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cores"} cores
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                      %mi Core
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %msub
                        %mi FinSet
                        %mi sk
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \big( Core(G FinSet_{sk})/_{X}, \sqcup, \times \big)
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GuillouMay11"} Guillou-May 11, Def. 1.3
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#BohmannOsorno14"} Bohmann-Osorno 14, Def. 1.4
          %h3#AsEnrichedInPermutativeCategories As enriched in permutative categories
          #AdditiveBurnsideCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PermCat"}> PermCat
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burnside+category"} Burnside category
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category+of+correspondences"} (2,1)-category of correspondences
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Corr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Corr(G FinSet)
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-categories"} equivalent
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
              and whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-categories"} hom-categories
              are the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutative+category"} permutative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cores"} cores
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skeleta"} skeleta
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+categories"} slice categories
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
              from Def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#PermutativeCategoryOfFiniteGSets"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source"} source
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/domain"} domain
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Corr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mi FinSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mi sk
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Corr(G FinSet)\big( S_1, S_2  \big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    Core(G FinSet_{sk}/_{S_1 \times S_2})
                    \\,.
            %p
              This locally skeletal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%282%2C1%29-category"} (2,1)-category
              is the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PermCat"}> PermCat
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
                Burnside category
              = succeed "_" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                      %msub
                        %mi Burn
                        %mi pc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Burn_{pc}
            %p
              It may be regarded as an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multicategory"} multicategory
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PermCat"} PermCat
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutative+categories"} permutative categories
              (a
              = succeed "-cateory" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi PC
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{PC}
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Guillout10"} Guillout 10
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#GuillouMay11"}> Guillou-May 11, Def. 1.6
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#BohmannOsorno14"} Bohmann-Osorno 14, Def. 7.1, 7.2
          %h3#AsEnrichedInabelianGroups As enriched in abelian groups
          #AdditiveBurnsideCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong (additive Burnside category)
            %p
              The
              %em additive Burnside category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi Burn
                      %mi ad
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Burn_{ad}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+category"} additive category
              obtained from the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PermCat"} PermCat
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
              Burnside category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi Burn
                      %mi pc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Burn_{pc}
              (Def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdditiveBurnsideCategory"}
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutative+category"} permutative category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Core
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi FinSet
                      %mi sk
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ×
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Core(G FinSet_{sk}/_{S_1 \times S_2})
              with its
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group"} Grothendieck group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion"} group completion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi PermCat
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mtext iso classes
                    %mi CMon
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi K
                    %mi Ab
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K \;\colon\; PermCat \overset{\text{iso classes}}{\longrightarrow} CMon \overset{K}{\longrightarrow} Ab
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Core
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %msub
                        %mi FinSet
                        %mi sk
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ×
                          %msub
                            %mi S
                            %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Core(G FinSet_{sk}/_{S_1 \times S_2})
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi Burn
                      %mi ab
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mo •
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi Burn
                      %mi pc
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G Burn_{ab}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    K_{\bullet} G Burn_{pc}
                    \\,.
          #BurnsideRingIsEndomorphismRingInBurnsideCategory.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burnside+ring"} Burnside ring
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism+ring"} endomorphism ring
                of additive Burnside category)
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism+ring"} endomorphism ring
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-set"} G-set
              (the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast
              equipped with the, necessarily,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+action"} trivial action
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdditiveBurnsideCategory"}
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burnside+ring"} Burnside ring
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A(G)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi End
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                        %msub
                          %mi Burn
                          %mi ad
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    End_{G Burn_{ad}}(\ast, \ast)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    A(G)
          %h3#EnrichedInSpectra As enriched in spectra
          #SpectralBurnsideCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              (
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spectra"}> Spectra
                \-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burnside+category"} Burnside category
            %p
              Since construction of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+spectra+of+permutative+categories"} K-theory spectra of permutative categories
              applies
              = succeed "-wise" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PermCat"} PermCat
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
              (
              %a{:href => "multifunctor#MonoidalFunctoriality"}> this Prop.
              )
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi PermCat
                    %mi Cat
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{K}_\bullet
                    \\;\colon\;
                    PermCat Cat \longrightarrow Spectra Cat
            %p
              the image of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PermCat"} PermCat
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Burnside+category"} Burnside category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G \mathcal{E}
              from Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AdditiveBurnsideCategory"}
              under forming
              = succeed "-wise" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-object"} hom-object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+spectra+of+permutative+categories"} K-theory spectra of permutative categories
              yields a
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spectra"} Spectra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi Burn
                      %mi sp
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝕂
                      %mo •
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi Burn
                      %mi pc
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G Burn_{sp}
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\mathbb{K}_\bullet G Burn_{pc}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is called the
              = succeed "." do
                %em spectral Burnside category
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#GuillouMay11"}> Guillou-May 11, Def. 1.12
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#BohmannOsorno14"} Bohmann-Osorno 14, Def. 7.3
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_spectra
            Relation to
            = succeed "-Spectra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          #GSpectraAreSpectralMackeyFunctors.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-spectra"} G-spectra
                are spectral presheaves on the spectral Burnside category)
            %p
              There is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zag"} zig-zag
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalences"} Quillen equivalences
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mi Burn
                      %mi sp
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Spectra
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Qu
                      %mi zigzag
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mi Spectra
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [ G Burn_{sp}, Spectra ]
                    \\;\simeq_{Qu}^{zigzag}\;
                    G Spectra
            %p
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+functors"} model category of
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spectra"} Spectra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+presheaves"} enriched presheaves
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+Burnside+category"} spectral Burnside category
              from Def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SpectralBurnsideCategory"}
              (“
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+Mackey+functors"}> spectral Mackey functors
              ”) and that of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genuine+G-spectra"} genuine G-spectra
            %p
              This equivalence is such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+Mackey+functor"} spectral Mackey functor
              corresponding to a fibrant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-spectrum"} G-spectrum
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              assigns to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transitive+action"} transitive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-set"} G-set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G/H
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+point+spectrum"} fixed point spectrum
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^H
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi G
                      %mn ∞
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi H
                    %mo ,
                    %mi E
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mi H
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G/H
                    \\;\mapsto\;
                    E(G/H)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    [\Sigma^\infty_G G/H, E]^G
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    E^H
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#GuillouMay11"}> GuillouMay 11, theorem 1.13, corollary 1.14, remark 2.5
            ).
